// E0408: a function that is one operation on its inputs --
// `fs_st_get(word[] st, int at) { word v = st[at]; } return word v;` is a second
// spelling of the language's own indexing, and the call site should say
// `st[at]` itself. It is the family of E0403 (a function returning only a
// constant), E0406 (a pure forwarder) and E0407, and like them it removes a name
// a reader has to open to learn it is nothing.
//
// The reduction (./shape.id, ./ops.id) substitutes each local into the
// expression that uses it; an operation is any node that is not a parameter, a
// literal or an `(import NAME)`. A function is a hit when its reduced expression
// is exactly one operation whose operands are parameters and imports only (a
// literal is a value that deserves a name, which a constant in conf.id gives it
// without a function), when nothing reads it as a function value, and when it is
// not a test fixture (./fixture.id). A function with control flow, or with a
// statement that is no part of the one expression, is never a hit.
//
// Each hit is reported as VALUE (the function returns the expression) or
// VOID-CALL (a void function whose one statement is a call).

wsc_scan() {
  if((import chkfail)[0] == 0) {
    wsc_loop();
  }
} return void;
